## Installation

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone <YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL>
cd CarCare_AI
```

### 2. Create the Virtual Environment

```bash
py -3.12 -m venv .venv
```

Activate it:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Start Ollama

Install Ollama and make sure the local service is running.

Pull the required model:

```bash
ollama pull llama3.2:3b
```

### 5. Start the Backend

```bash
python -m uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Open:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000/
```

---

## Project Scope

The current system is designed around:

```text
Vehicle Part Identification
            +
Maintenance Information Retrieval
            +
Document-Grounded Answer Generation
```

The Computer Vision model identifies visible vehicle parts.

It does not directly diagnose mechanical faults from an image.

For example:

```text
Image
  ↓
Wheel detected
```

rather than:

```text
Image
  ↓
Wheel bearing failure diagnosed
```

The maintenance guidance is generated from the retrieved information in the maintenance document.

